      "publication_revision": null,
      "text_revision": null,
      "target_revision": null,
      "timestamp_seconds": null,
      "original_text": "\"Very well.\" Tuppence helped herself liberally to buttered toast and gave the abridged biography of Miss Prudence Cowley, fifth daughter of Archdeacon Cowley of Little Missendell, Suffolk: ward duties, plate-washing, peeling potatoes, sweeping out wards (where she found a friend of her childhood in Lieutenant Thomas Beresford\u2014bow, Tommy!), then a trade van, a motor-lorry, and a young general. \"After that, a Government office, and several enjoyable tea parties\u2014until I was combed out at last. Since then I've been looking for a job. Now\u2014your turn.\"",
