            "original_text": "\"Very well.\" Tuppence helped herself liberally to buttered toast and gave the abridged biography of Miss Prudence Cowley, fifth daughter of Archdeacon Cowley of Little Missendell, Suffolk: ward duties, plate-washing, peeling potatoes, sweeping out wards (where she found a friend of her childhood in Lieutenant Thomas Beresford\u2014bow, Tommy!), then a trade van, a motor-lorry, and a young general. \"After that, a Government office, and several enjoyable tea parties\u2014until I was combed out at last. Since then I've been looking for a job. Now\u2014your turn.\"",
            "primary_target": 0,
            "targets": [
              {
                "draft_para": 13,
                "text": "\"Very well.\" Tuppence helped herself liberally to buttered toast and gave the abridged biography of Miss Prudence Cowley, fifth daughter of Archdeacon Cowley of Little Missendell, Suffolk: she came up to London to an officers' hospital, where she did ward duties, plate-washing, peeling potatoes, sweeping out wards (where she found a friend of her childhood in Lieutenant Thomas Beresford\u2014bow, Tommy!), then a trade van, a motor-lorry, and a young general. \"After that, a Government office, and several enjoyable tea parties\u2014until I was combed out at last. Since then I've been looking for a job. Now\u2014your turn.\""
              }
            ]
          }
        }
